s://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:32:14-07:00","id":905144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=905116#post905116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...not sure what's with the kinda aggressive response, but ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you did describe our review as &quot;savage&quot; and it is more a case of other people who may listen to go in knowing we are just being fair, and not being harsh for the sake of it. That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - The Premier World of Darkness Podcast<br /> Co-designer and miniature painter for Noble Armada 3e<br /> Staff writer for CYBR Magazine <a href=\"https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/</a><br /> Writer, developer, editor, layout for Darker Days Radio Publishing<br /> Writer for Cubicle 7 Wrath and Glory Revised","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T16:00:54-07:00","id":905238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr Ether</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=905144#post905144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you did describe our review as &quot;savage&quot; and it is more a case of other people who may listen to go in knowing we are just being fair, and not being harsh for the sake of it. That's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>...in which I ended my statement with &quot;savage, yo&quot; which I would think leads the impression that I'm joking. But ok. <br /> <br /> As for not being harsh for the sake of it...the mocking tone throughout the review says otherwise to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T16:33:50-07:00","id":905253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=905238#post905238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...in which I ended my statement with &quot;savage, yo&quot; which I would think leads the impression that I'm joking. But ok.<br /> <br /> As for not being harsh for the sake of it...the mocking tone throughout the review says otherwise to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mocking? No. Disappointed given how much we liked Demon and previous works. Yes. Plus by the end of the review we were just glad to have finished this episode knowing it would take a long time to tackle just one book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - The Premier World of Darkness Podcast<br /> Co-designer and miniature painter for Noble Armada 3e<br /> Staff writer for CYBR Magazine <a href=\"https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/</a><br /> Writer, developer, editor, layout for Darker Days Radio Publishing<br /> Writer for Cubicle 7 Wrath and Glory Revised","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:54:05-07:00","id":905973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr Ether</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=905253#post905253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mocking? No. Disappointed given how much we liked Demon and previous works. Yes. Plus by the end of the review we were just glad to have finished this episode knowing it would take a long time to tackle just one book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disappointing? Vast understatement if the final verdict is declaring that the game is unsalvageable and to not bother purchasing it at all. <br /> <br /> Says a lot more to me then just &quot;disappointing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T11:17:41-07:00","id":908451,"title":"","content":"yeah, honestly, this is the most disappointing episode of Darker Days I have listened to. Very shallow, biased and reductive reading of the text. Lacking a lot of accuracy as well.<br /> <br /> And definitely mocking in tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:05:16-07:00","id":908725,"title":"","content":"To be honest I feel that everyone is entitled to their opinion and that different games will appeal more to some than others. The disappointing thing with this episode is that everyone seemed to find the game line unappealing. I couldn't tell from the review if the game line is any good, just that it didn't sit well with the reviewers.<br /> <br /> The worst thing was the comment stating &quot;don't buy this&quot;, &quot;don't support this&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have read other reviews of the book which differ from this, so I can't help feeling this may be more opinion on the themes involved than the quality of the game line.<br /> <br /> I backed the kickstarter without reading any of the uploaded text, so I will be able to form my own opinion once I get my book. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/142-thiassi","name":"Thiassi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T18:48:27-07:00","id":918359,"title":"","content":"That Podcast saved me some money. They reaffirmed what others had told me about BtP. Some may think it was rough but sometimes the truth stings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T03:46:26-07:00","id":918535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiassi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=908725#post908725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I feel that everyone is entitled to their opinion and that different games will appeal more to some than others. The disappointing thing with this episode is that everyone seemed to find the game line unappealing. I couldn't tell from the review if the game line is any good, just that it didn't sit well with the reviewers.<br /> <br /> The worst thing was the comment stating &quot;don't buy this&quot;, &quot;don't support this&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have read other reviews of the book which differ from this, so I can't help feeling this may be more opinion on the themes involved than the quality of the game line.<br /> <br /> I backed the kickstarter without reading any of the uploaded text, so I will be able to form my own opinion once I get my book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given how much we generally love the CofD line of books, and have in the past felt even such steaming piles of mess, like WoD Gypsies, could be rescued, let me say that the entire DD crew is very disappointed in Beast, with the concept, the way the changes were done in a superficial manner leaving a book that reads in a very confused manner, with the connotations the concept has for certain groups, how shallow the game feels, and how critique of the game was met and dismissed.<br /> <br /> We are certainly upset because we have always, always tried to find the positive in a game or book. This is a complete first on our part.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, sure there are a few interesting things in the game, but those alone are not enough to warrent buying the game in our opinion. I have my own personal opinions of fixes to Beast, but that involves a lot of gutting of the core setting.<br /> <br /> And finally, we quoted large parts of the game book. We were not reading from the original draft of the game. We had both versions and compared them side by side. We did a lot of reading and thinking and talking behind the scenes in order to present an honest review, and a review that focused as much on the game without attacking anyone. But, it was hard when for one of the team Beast presents some very serious issues that feel personally insulting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - The Premier World of Darkness Podcast<br /> Co-designer and miniature painter for Noble Armada 3e<br /> Staff writer for CYBR Magazine <a href=\"https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/</a><br /> Writer, developer, editor, layout for Darker Days Radio Publishing<br /> Writer for Cubicle 7 Wrath and Glory Revised","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T04:23:43-07:00","id":918547,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to chime in with my support for the review. It seemed fair and on the whole I agree with the criticisms made. In addition I found the tone of the review to be entertaining, and even though I have read Beast a long time ago* and already formed my opinion I still enjoyed the review enough for it to be worth listening too the whole thing.<br /> <br /> * Short version - I like using Beasts as antagonists, and I feel that doing so resulted in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters\">some of my best work</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-21-2016, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T08:16:06-07:00","id":918631,"title":"","content":"So I've got a lot of feelings about the review, and how people have responded to it, and the game itself. I'm going to try to write all of my thoughts up in a way that's hopefully concise and follows from point to point, but it's gonna be a long post.<br /> <br /> <b>Characters that you Hate</b><br /> <br /> I don't know if everybody's familiar with the TV series <i>Archer</i>. It's a comedy about a bunch of spies working for a government agency. It's mostly about their interpersonal relationships and <i>how awful they are as people</i>. Anybody who thinks &quot;Man, I'd love to be Archer/Lana/whomever.&quot; is either saying that they want to be a petty, vain, asshole or that they don't <i>get</i> the show. The creator himself has said that he wouldn't want <i>any</i> of the characters as friends. There are a lot of classic, popular shows like this: <i>Seinfeld</i>, <i>It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia</i>, <i>Friends</i>, the list goes on. <i>Beast</i> is sort of like that: The characters, more than almost any other CofD line, come across as the meanest, most petty. Granted, this is partially because some assholes subscribe to a &quot;You're whoever you are on your worst day&quot; mentality, so a Begotten is never treated as more than their most petty, small-time feeding. Or for whatever reason, people make a big deal out of their big meals.<br /> <br /> The part of the review where I realized I wasn't going to agree with them is when they asked &quot;Who would want to play as one of them?&quot; and &quot;Who could ever think a beast is a good person?&quot; Because those questions <b><i>miss the point</i></b>.* And it surprised me because y'all are such big fans of the CofD, because none of the games are designed with the assumption that people are going to want to make sympathetic, good characters (even Hunter). The entire Chronicles of Darkness system is based around personal horror. Beast is the logical extreme of that assumption: these characters are assholes. The <i>point</i> of it all, the <i>main draw</i> of this game -- for me at least -- is that more than any other game, beasts are set up to be awful people. The beauty of the game is that I can do whatever I want from there. All of the Children I've made so far are people who have really unfortunate urges trying to leverage their urges in productive, or at least non-destructive ways. But nothing about the game says that I have to make them that way. I could also make a character who goes straight-up Patrick Bateman, Hannibal Lecter, or Pamela Vorhees. There's no judgment either way. And as a player, I think this is a great thing.<br /> <br /> *The point being that not all games assume that people want to be the characters they're playing. I don't want to be <i>any</i> of the characters that I play in either my WoD or CofD games. Maybe my Scion character, though she's had to suffer all of her friends and family dying except for the other PCs.<br /> <br /> Does the book act like Begotten are hot shit? Of course! So does Vampire: The Requiem 2E. It's like it was written by an Anne Rice fan who found out vampires are real and got Embraced and is dead and loving it. Werewolf makes it sound like being an Uratha is nothing short of high-octane awesomeness. It's the job of these books to try to sell the reader on wanting to play their subjects. But that's <i>not</i> the same thing as wanting to <i>be</i> the characters. The most relevant quote from the book is from the Introduction:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: The Primordial, page 18, &quot;No Neat Little Boxes&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are not \u201cgood guys.\u201d They terrify people in order to feed their Horrors. Although their culture teaches that they do so in order to impart important lessons, their peculiar form of pedagogy is entirely optional. A Beast is capable of being a force for wisdom, even for \u201cgood\u201d in the Chronicles of Darkness, but doing so is entirely up to the Beast. Likewise, a Beast\u2019s primary enemy, the Hero, believes that killing the Beast is the right, objectively moral thing to do. The Beast disagrees. <i>Neither of them is necessarily wrong</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>People reading this book should be keeping this in mind even when the book is going on about how awesome Lairs are, and how Beasts are inheritors to awesome responsibility and legacy, and etc...etc....<br /> <br /> <b>No Metaphor Stands Up to Scrutiny</b><br /> <br /> Hey, I get some people being uncomfortable about the LGBT subtext. But I can name some other popular franchises that act as metaphors for real-world oppressed groups: <i>X-Men</i> and <i>True Blood</i>. The vampires of the Sookieverse are quite obviously stand-ins for the LGBT community, but they're also literally blood-sucking monsters, even the ones who seem sympathetic at first. <i>X-Men</i>'s classic movers and shakers, Professor X and Magneto, are stand-ins for Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr. and Malcolm X. But that falls apart because Professor X raises child soldiers in a cult-like environment, and Magneto is a genocidal tyrant. But we can still borrow elements from the real world to help sell an idea, even if it's not perfect.<br /> <br /> The closest that Beast as a game gets to saying &quot;Beasts are an oppressed minority&quot; is &quot;The majority tries to put all Beasts in the &quot;Evil monster&quot; box because it fits their narrative, and some try to enact simple, violent solutions to the &quot;beast problem.&quot; Beast's disagree.&quot; I get that some players will also disagree, that was made <i>very</i> clear to me when I read RPG.net's threads about Beast. And if that's the case, then Beast isn't the game for you. This isn't a bad thing, no game is for everybody. The issue I have is when people make bullshit claims like, &quot;There's nothing redeeming about this&quot; or &quot;This is an objective statement about the game's quality, we're just being honest.&quot; when it's clearly an issue of preference.<br /> <br /> <b>Heroes, The Monomyth, and Subversion vs Aversion</b><br /> <br /> So there was a line in the review where one of the hosts said, &quot;You can't go on and on about the monomyth and then tell the Storyteller to just ignore it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why not? The whole point is that the monomyth has no bearing on the real world, and Heroes are just random assholes who show up thinking that Beasts need to die. There's no great narrative that Beasts are a part of. Same with Heroes.<br /> <br /> Hey, let's talk about Subversion vs Aversion. Beast <i>averts</i> the monomyth by asserting that Beasts are more than just the &quot;boss monster&quot; for the Hero to slay. In play, you're just playing people trying to survive. Nothing epic or grand here. Antagonistic Heroes <i>think</i> they're part of a monomyth, and so from a Hero's perspective when they show up to slay the beast thinking it's all part of a bigger narrative it's a subversion. Hence the Subversion parts of the book. But from a Beast perspective, it's an <i>A</i>version because Beasts know that they're not a part of a greater narrative.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Heroes, one of the issues the book has is shutting down the idea of friendly Heroes. But it also works into the &quot;default Beast story&quot;, which I approve the game of having. Like, nobody's gonna stop you from having a Beast/Hero buddy cop story -- <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-the-nwod?p=861253#post861253\">I made a post about the TV series <i>Lucifer</i> and how it could work as a Beast game</a> -- but that's not the intent. There's nothing wrong with an author saying, &quot;I want you to play my game in a specific way.&quot; Matt thinks that allowing playable Heroes and introducing sympathetic, friendly Heroes goes against the intent of the game. There's nothing wrong with that. The four example Heroes are fantastic because they're (mostly) sympathetic, but unlikely to be friendly. Even the MRA one is fine, because they wanted an example of somebody we could all hate without feeling <i>too</i> bad.<br /> <br /> Put another way: Strix are supposed to be used as Enemy Within antagonists who tear a vampiric society apart from the inside thanks to propaganda and preying on Kindred fears. But they're powerful enough that honestly you could have a Strix who just possesses a Kindred, or an Uratha, or whatever, and works its way through Kindred society just murdering them all like Jason. The books give you advice on how to use them as subversive, guerilla monsters that tear things apart. The intent is to use them in a specific way. Same here with Heroes.<br /> <br /> And again, that can be not to your liking: I know lots of people who hate it when games tell them what kind of games to play, or what stories to tell. But that's a preference issue.<br /> <br /> <b>Wrapping it Up</b><br /> <br /> So yeah, this went long. But I hope it explains my disappointment with the review. The book probably needed another editorial pass: it's got some inconsistencies that need addressing, particularly when it comes to how the book treats Lessons. But saying that there's <i>nothing</i> redeemable and calling for people to boycott buying it is...it's not the objective &quot;Let's talk about the real problems.&quot; review that you guys claim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 06-21-2016, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T08:56:24-07:00","id":918646,"title":"","content":"For me personally, I don't need to play or have players play good guys. But the character has to be sympathetic. Beasts to me are not. They do evil things. Either because they were born that way, and then bemoan those who wish to stop them (and then we are told in a matter fact way Heroes are wrong - I am of the school of moral grey areas in all parts of CofD, since this is why I don't play WoD anymore). Or they chose to be a Beast, because they were ostracised for some reason from society, and so feel the right to then do awful things - which in turn to me makes them more awful and unsympathetic. And lessons is this thing tacked out to stroke those egos. As much as I like running games and playing through stories of moral choices and seeing the descent to evil, playing out and out monsters is not fun.<br /> <br /> As any long time listener to the show would know, they know the sorts of games we run and stories we run. And thus if they like that, and understand our position in reviews, then they should also understand the dislike of this game we have, and our dislike at how the rewrite was handled and the fanbase was managed. As a backer, I am angry more wasn't done to address those concerns. That is where the anger comes from.<br /> <br /> If however, you feel that the game is not for us, then our review still stands. If people like the types of games we like, then our review is valid for helping them make an informed decision. Not all games are made equal. The choice is still yours.<br /> <br /> If you then feel the need to sell the game to us still, and be a cheer leader for it, that says more about strength of your own conviction for the game. I fully acknowledge people dislike Requiem, but I will only do the hard sell if their dislike is from a position of ignorance, or worse some sort of edition war elitism, not if they simply say, that they prefer the style of the one over the other.<br /> <br /> Ultimately you can feel disappointed in our review, but we are allowed to be disappointed and angry too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - The Premier World of Darkness Podcast<br /> Co-designer and miniature painter for Noble Armada 3e<br /> Staff writer for CYBR Magazine <a href=\"https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/</a><br /> Writer, developer, editor, layout for Darker Days Radio Publishing<br /> Writer for Cubicle 7 Wrath and Glory Revised","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T05:53:55-07:00","id":919054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr Ether</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=918646#post918646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me personally, I don't need to play or have players play good guys. But the character has to be sympathetic. Beasts to me are not. They do evil things. Either because they were born that way, and then bemoan those who wish to stop them (and then we are told in a matter fact way Heroes are wrong - I am of the school of moral grey areas in all parts of CofD, since this is why I don't play WoD anymore). Or they chose to be a Beast, because they were ostracised for some reason from society, and so feel the right to then do awful things - which in turn to me makes them more awful and unsympathetic. And lessons is this thing tacked out to stroke those egos. As much as I like running games and playing through stories of moral choices and seeing the descent to evil, playing out and out monsters is not fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of why I don't get this paragraph is that it's patently untrue, and that should be obvious from reading the book. The &quot;No Neat Little Boxes&quot; explicitly says, &quot;There are no easy answers here.&quot; Beasts aren't wrong. Heroes aren't wrong. If it says somewhere else that Beasts are definitely good, and are the Real Victims in all of this, then that's a failure of the book, but that's the sort of thing that requires another editing pass, not writing the book off as irredeemable.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I don't see how Beasts are less sympathetic as a whole than vampires. They angst less about their condition, is that it? And then try to justify their urges after the fact with the lessons bullshit? I thought you guys &quot;got it&quot; when one of you mentioned playing heroic Beasts like Dexter, but that apparently was either sarcasm or not enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr Ether</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=918646#post918646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you then feel the need to sell the game to us still, and be a cheer leader for it, that says more about strength of your own conviction for the game. I fully acknowledge people dislike Requiem, but I will only do the hard sell if their dislike is from a position of ignorance, or worse some sort of edition war elitism, not if they simply say, that they prefer the style of the one over the other.<br /> <br /> Ultimately you can feel disappointed in our review, but we are allowed to be disappointed and angry too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately I don't care if you feel like the game isn't for you, but I think there's a lot of incorrect conclusions you're jumping to. Like how you mentioned that the writer of Demon did both, and made the comment that Demons aren't kin with Beasts because he didn't want Demons to be tainted by association. That was probably the most infuriating quote from the podcast, and it definitely changed my opinion of y'all. (Fun fact: Matt's also the writer for Promethean 2E, and Beasts are the only supernatural template explicitly immune to Disquiet. Curious how that makes you feel.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 06-22-2016, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T11:18:30-07:00","id":920458,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rather than have Chris speak for all of us, I'll chime in here myself. Hi, I'm Matt, and I did most of the heavy lifting on the Beast review.<br /> <br /> The problem with the \u201cNo Neat Little Boxes\u201d Paragraph is that the rest of the book more or less ignores it. If Clanbook Baali opened up with a disclaimer saying that they were actually really nice people would that make the rest of the book any less horrific? There are no examples given in the book of a Beast helping someone out through their feeding. There are no examples given in the book of a person\u2019s life being meaningfully improved by a Beast\u2019s Existence. There are, however, several times given when Heroes are demonized. The book equates them to Gamergate, MRA\u2019s, and Internet Trolls. It describes their mindset in absolute terms. More importantly it also states that they were born this way and actually changing their mind is a monumental task compared to just killing the poor fuckers. Meanwhile the \u201cGood\u201d Heroes are so amazingly uninteresting the book says not to use them and doesn\u2019t provide rules for them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The reason why Beasts aren\u2019t sympathetic is that the book doesn\u2019t portray them as such. There isn\u2019t really any evidence of Beasts fighting against their darker nature, they embrace it wholeheartedly. Instead being a Beast is described as the most amazing thing ever with only the slight downside of summoning acceptable murder targets whenever you don\u2019t keep your hunger in check. (You yourself said that you loved the gamergate guy because you were \u2018allowed\u2019 to hate him). And Dexter is an example of a \u201cGood Beast\u201d But he\u2019s a very narrow one. Also Dexter owns up to his own aberrant nature and monstrosity, and doesn\u2019t once even hint at \u2018teaching lessons\u2019. He\u2019s not putting the bodies on display, he\u2019s not making examples of them, he\u2019s removing them from the equation so that the rest of society can keep on turning.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As for my assumption about Demon. Giving Beasts and Demon no mechanical interaction beyond enforced antagonism is a pretty good indicator that you don\u2019t want them to interact. Which goes against the \u201cNo Little Boxes\u201d thing yet again. Beasts hate Demons and Demons hate Beasts end of story.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As far as Promethean\u2019s the fiction anthology is fairly explicit that having a Beast in their life is actively detrimental to the Promethean. Beasts are cheerleaders of the inhuman, they want to drive Prometheans to become the world destroying monsters they were \u2018meant\u2019 to be. Sure that creates conflict and extends the game length but I\u2019m not sure why, in character, a Promethean would continue to willingly associate with the creepy guy that keeps insisting you should go kill some conservative soccer moms who hate him. The fact that they\u2019re immune to disquiet should be a giant red flag to the Promethean of just how inhuman they are.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12026-matt-darker-days","name":"Matt-Darker Days","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:48:17-07:00","id":931460,"title":"","content":"I would love to hear an episode about how you guys do horror in your games. What works for you, what doesn't. And more than anything a podcast dedicated to playing vanilla core Chronicle of Darkness mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:53:33-07:00","id":931462,"title":"","content":"I like Beast mechanically because of the lair and horror merging powers, but I totally understand why you don't like the tone. Who just says that MRA's and Gamergate are purely bad? Thats like saying that feminist are all bad, or that hobbiest are bad for keeping unwanted influence out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:31:19-07:00","id":931482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=931460#post931460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to hear an episode about how you guys do horror in your games. What works for you, what doesn't. And more than anything a podcast dedicated to playing vanilla core Chronicle of Darkness mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vanilla core Cof you say. Well you should check out our spinoff podcast Network Zero.<a href=\"http://networkzero.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://networkzero.podbean.com/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - The Premier World of Darkness Podcast<br /> Co-designer and miniature painter for Noble Armada 3e<br /> Staff writer for CYBR Magazine <a href=\"https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/</a><br /> Writer, developer, editor, layout for Darker Days Radio Publishing<br /> Writer for Cubicle 7 Wrath and Glory Revised","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T13:50:40-07:00","id":932623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr Ether</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=931482#post931482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vanilla core Cof you say. Well you should check out our spinoff podcast Network Zero.<a href=\"http://networkzero.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://networkzero.podbean.com/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Already a fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:05:35-07:00","id":993787,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Darker Days is proud to present Episode #73!<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> This evening we cover Charnel Houses of Europe. It's a tough episode, but we're proud to have done it.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/darker-days-radio-episode-73/\" target=\"_blank\">http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/dar...io-episode-73/</a><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T06:10:53-07:00","id":994006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr Ether</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/438-darker-days-radio?p=918646#post918646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me personally, I don't need to play or have players play good guys. But the character has to be sympathetic. Beasts to me are not. They do evil things. Either because they were born that way, and then bemoan those who wish to stop them (and then we are told in a matter fact way Heroes are wrong - I am of the school of moral grey areas in all parts of CofD, since this is why I don't play WoD anymore). Or they chose to be a Beast, because they were ostracised for some reason from society, and so feel the right to then do awful things - which in turn to me makes them more awful and unsympathetic. And lessons is this thing tacked out to stroke those egos. As much as I like running games and playing through stories of moral choices and seeing the descent to evil, playing out and out monsters is not fun.<br /> <br /> As any long time listener to the show would know, they know the sorts of games we run and stories we run. And thus if they like that, and understand our position in reviews, then they should also understand the dislike of this game we have, and our dislike at how the rewrite was handled and the fanbase was managed. As a backer, I am angry more wasn't done to address those concerns. That is where the anger comes from.<br /> <br /> If however, you feel that the game is not for us, then our review still stands. If people like the types of games we like, then our review is valid for helping them make an informed decision. Not all games are made equal. The choice is still yours.<br /> <br /> If you then feel the need to sell the game to us still, and be a cheer leader for it, that says more about strength of your own conviction for the game. I fully acknowledge people dislike Requiem, but I will only do the hard sell if their dislike is from a position of ignorance, or worse some sort of edition war elitism, not if they simply say, that they prefer the style of the one over the other.<br /> <br /> Ultimately you can feel disappointed in our review, but we are allowed to be disappointed and angry too.</div> </div> </div> </div> Quick and easy way of getting to a more moral grey area is to have them focus on family feast, its easier to have them as &quot;good&quot; guy by allying with another Supernatural being they can scanvege from, and then play up their relief at being saved from having to torment people, by becoming incredibly loyal, attached, and perhaps obsessed with the being that allows them to feed in a more humane way.<br /> <br /> But personally, outside of playing in a crossover, I'd likely play a beast as what it normally is, the most sadistic fuck in CoD, someone with a layer of hell for a soul with a horror moving through it. I'd embrace the poor evil as what makes it unique from more naunanced evils like Vampire, Changeling, Demon, ect...<br /> <br /> Beast doesn't bothered with angst, its best to use as a safe way to explore you darkest side, unapologetically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:25:42-07:00","id":994154,"title":"","content":"I went searching through the PDF text for an MRA reference, couldn't find one, searched the internet for some context on the MRA hero connect, because honest as an actual MRA I didn't see it.<br /> <br /> There was one gamergate reference in a previous draft, which got nixed and one of the heroes is seen as a stand in for an MRAs by some which I had a good laugh about as that hero is described as seeing himself as chiveralous and MRAs tend to have distain for historical chivelary, which was an emotionally abusive and exploit idea in its historical context.<br /> <br /> Also being a Gamergater and MRA aren't the samething, while I'm sympathic to gameegate or parts of it, I had nothing to do with it and did not particapate in it.<br /> <br /> Honestly as an MRA I find it all very funny. The idea that we're literally the fucking template for the literal heroes of the game fighting Beasts that terrorize people and feed on their fear, and yet somehow, were the bad guys anyways, and the Beast tormenting people is the good guy, is enough to send me into giggles. Not saying that the connection is there any more, it got written out, but again as an MRA I find it hugely entertaining. Almost makes me want play a Hero honestly. Even with discouraging it, its absolutely do able.<br /> <br /> As an MRA I'm not so hypersensitive as to be worried about it. I like the game system, I like lairs, and I like the flexiblity. I can play a good guy who buddies up with another type of monster, to help them make some kind of peace with themselves and find balance.<br /> <br /> Or I can play a royal sadistic bastard who kidnaps people to its layer to torture and feed on their terror, till they can't be mentally broken anymore, at which point it disguards them for a fresh victim, who actually prefers to target heroes because they make more durable toys.<br /> <br /> The BDSM connection on the other hand I can see, abit BDSM fantasies, but not BDSM practices obviously (hypothetically you could find a mascotist who agrees to be terrorisze and have their fears played on, for sexually pleasure).<br /> <br /> I gave the game 5 stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T18:14:34-07:00","id":995462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphall